 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Physiotherapeutic exercises in the supine position (Table 1 descriptions), few general instructions, performed over ~5 years of follow-up.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model each patient lying relaxed supine and record the resting resultant force at the implant level (L1; L3 for WP5)",
   "Simulate: (1) lifting one straight leg, (2) lifting both straight legs, (3) lifting the pelvis (bridging); no external load",
   "Report the peak resultant force during each exercise minus the resting value (N)",
   "A whole-spine MSK model outputs total segment compression at the implant level, not the implant share; compare trends/relative changes unless the model includes the VBR and posterior fixator; ranking (one leg ~10 N << both legs ~220 N < bridging ~250 N) is the main target"
  ],
